+# BLUE CURRENT V49.5.0 — ROLLOUT ACTIVATION CONTROL
+
+V49 begins Blue Current scale operations.
+
+## V49.01–V49.05
+
+The first V49 wave converts a V48 rollout plan into an explicit per-location activation review.
+
+Blue Current now evaluates each planned restaurant against live operating conditions before a human approves it for activation.
+
+### Live activation preflight
+Each planned location is checked for:
+
+1. inclusion in the signed human EXPAND scope
+2. inclusion in the current rollout plan
+3. current readiness at or above the rollout plan readiness floor
+4. no High/Critical leadership-attention state
+5. no urgent predictive intervention requiring immediate leadership action
+
+The preflight is recalculated from current operating data.
+
+### Human activation approval
+
+Adds:
+
+`POST /api/rollout-activation-control/locations/:locationId/approve`
+
+Approval requires:
+- authenticated admin permission
+- explicit approver
+- location inside authorized scope
+- current rollout-plan membership
+
+If all gates pass, the administrator can approve the location for activation.
+
+If one or more gates are open, approval is blocked unless a documented executive override reason is supplied.
+
+### Important state separation
+
+Approval does not mean deployment.
+
+Approved locations are written as:
+
+- `status: APPROVED_FOR_ACTIVATION`
+- `deploymentState: NOT_DEPLOYED`
+- rollout location state: `APPROVED_FOR_ACTIVATION`
+
+Blue Current records that leadership approved activation but does not perform technical deployment.
+
+### Activation ledger
+
+Each approval records:
+- organization
+- rollout plan
+- location
+- rollout wave
+- approver
+- authenticated actor
+- timestamp
+- complete preflight snapshot
+- whether an override was used
+- override reason
+- approval note
+- deployment state
+
+The event is also audited and published to realtime listeners.
+
+## Policy
+
+- `explicitHumanApprovalRequired: true`
+- `adminApprovalRequired: true`
+- `overrideRequiresReason: true`
+- `approvalDoesNotDeploy: true`
+- `automaticApproval: false`
+- `automaticDeployment: false`
+- `automaticActivation: false`
+
+## Current authenticated runtime
+
+The current untouched Chefs runtime does not yet contain a signed rollout plan.
+
+The V49 endpoint therefore correctly reports:
+
+- status: `rollout-plan-required`
+- locations under activation review: 0
+- automatic approval: false
+- automatic deployment: false
+- automatic activation: false
+
+The current demo owner account is not an admin, so an attempted activation approval correctly returns HTTP 403.
+
+## Validation
+
+- V49.5 focused activation lifecycle PASS
+- live preflight calculation PASS
+- open-gate approval blocked without override PASS
+- documented executive override PASS
+- approved-for-activation state PASS
+- deployment remains NOT_DEPLOYED PASS
+- V48.30 certification regression PASS
+- authenticated V49.5 GET PASS
+- admin-only activation approval boundary PASS
+- authoritative database unchanged
+- npm run check PASS
+- 884 JavaScript files
+- 748 client scripts
+- 5,570 unique HTML IDs
+
+## Next
+
+V49.06–V49.10 should build Technical Activation Readiness:
+- integration/configuration checklist per location
+- authentication and user readiness
+- data-source connectivity state
+- reservation/floor/kitchen/workforce module readiness
+- launch blockers
+- technical activation packet
+- explicit human go-live authorization
+- no automatic production cutover
